# Report writing structure (QSLP-AE reference)

**Voice and tone:** [`oliver-thesis-plos-writing.mdc`](oliver-thesis-plos-writing.mdc) — thesis-derived British prose, mechanistic Results, validation-ladder thinking. **This file** covers section templates, word budget, and QSLP *explanation discipline* only.

**Reference paper:** Ciudad et al., *Aligning human and mouse EEG representations of sleep stages with a quadruplet split latent permutation auto-encoder* ([OpenReview K3Z4jVHUnf](https://openreview.net/pdf?id=K3Z4jVHUnf), ICLR 2026 Re-Align workshop). Same MSSV cohort, shared supervisors (Mørup, Kornum). Full text extract: [`docs/paper/source_extraction/qslp_ae_reference.txt`](docs/paper/source_extraction/qslp_ae_reference.txt).

**Our manuscript:** [`docs/paper/plos_my_paper.tex`](docs/paper/plos_my_paper.tex) — structure in [`report_outline.md`](report_outline.md).

**PLOS LaTeX formatting** remains governed by [`plos-compbiol-tex.mdc`](plos-compbiol-tex.mdc). This rule governs **prose quality and explanatory structure**, not template mechanics.

## Word budget

| | Words |
|---|------:|
| **Target** | 3,000–3,500 |
| **Hard cap** | 4,000 main text |
| **Count** | `cd docs/paper && texcount -inc -1 plos_my_paper.tex` |

Full breakdown: [`word_budget.md`](word_budget.md). **Methods ~1,100 w is enough.** Add words in **Results and Discussion** only until the adequacy checklist passes. Move detail to SI rather than exceed 4,000.

**Concision rules:** one idea per paragraph (3–5 sentences); no duplicate definitions; cite Fig/Table/SI instead of re-explaining; cut any sentence that does not add a number, protocol step, or interpretation.

