## What makes the reference paper readable

| Pattern | Example from QSLP-AE | Apply to our report |
|---------|----------------------|---------------------|
| **Problem → need → approach** | Rodent–human gap → “need for modeling procedures…” → QSLP-AE | Rose cross-lab gap → need for zero-shot holdout → decoder-only cHMM–GMVAE ladder |
| **Concrete DATA before METHODS** | 92 mice, 5 labs, 4 s epochs, label merge rules, PSD $\in \mathbb{R}^{128}$, EMG RMS | MSSV labs 2/3/5, Artifact removal, spectral tensor shape, per-lab locks — **numbers first** |
| **Build on prior work, state delta** | “Our model builds on… We modify… to use PSDs instead of raw signals” | “Extends thesis cGMVAE… decoder-only conditioning replaces encoder+decoder… sticky HMM–GMM replaces two-step MAR-HMM” |
| **Conceptual rename map** | style = individual/species, task = sleep stage | nuisance = subject/lab/montage, macro = Wake/NREM/REM, substage = mixture component |
| **Figure-first Methods** | Fig 1 panels (a)(b)(c) walk through training before equations | Fig 1: cohort split, train vs holdout path, ladder rungs — cite panel in prose |
| **One key equation when needed** | Loss $\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{QSLP}}$ after verbal setup | NMI \eqref{eq:nmi} after defining partitions $Y$, $\hat{Y}$ |
| **Metrics defined before Results** | Four probes S-on-S, T-on-T, T-on-S, S-on-T with direction arrows | Prior NMI, best-of-3 seeds, joint vs within-lab scopes — define before Table 1 |
| **Results interpret immediately** | “In Table 1, the baseline shows… Remarkably,… Regarding disentanglement,…” | “In Table 1, cHMM–GMVAE exceeds cGMVAE on every fold… Fold 2 is an exception because…” |
| **Honest limitations inline** | “task information leaks… probably due to…” | Seed fragility, K=3 macro ladder vs K-sweep, front-end locks not per-mouse |
| **Quantitative anchors** | Random 33%, $d_s=16$, $d_t=2$, mean ± SEM | NMI 0.56 vs 0.33, $\Delta=+0.22$, fold ranges, $K \in \{3,\ldots,15\}$ |
| **Appendix for overflow** | Dataset overview A.1, architecture A.5, probes A.6 | SI: thesis K=13, ablations, full within-lab table, locked YAML |

