## Section templates (our report)

Canonical order: **Abstract → Introduction → Data → Methods → Results and discussion → Conclusion → Acknowledgments → References → Appendix.** See [`report_outline.md`](report_outline.md).

### Introduction (350–450 words)

1. **Clinical / methodological problem** — Rose 2026 cross-lab scoring disagreement; supervised models fail across MSSV sites without retraining.
2. **Why unsupervised + temporal structure** — bout dynamics, substages, label noise as feature not bug.
3. **Gap vs prior work** — one sentence each on AccuSleep (transductive), SegWay (per-mouse), mcRBM (no holdout protocol); **our combination** in one sentence.
4. **Contributions as numbered list** — (i) decoder-only zero-shot holdout, (ii) fair ladder, (iii) substage biology after K-sweep. Point to Methods for protocol detail.

### Data (~300–400 words)

Use `\methodpara{Dataset.}`, `\methodpara{Epoch construction.}`, `\methodpara{Input representation.}` — numbers first, no model detail.

### Methods (3 subsections, ~900–1,100 words)

| Subsection | Bold starters |
|------------|---------------|
| Cross-validation and holdout protocol | Evaluation scopes. Holdout inference. Agreement metrics. |
| Model ladder and architecture | Model ladder. Encoder–decoder. Latent priors. |
| Training, substages, and reproducibility | Decoder-only conditioning. Training and checkpoints. Substage sweep. Data and code. |

**Fig 1** in Methods (protocol + ladder). Each block: `\methodpara{Label.}` then prose.

### Results and discussion (~900–1,100 words, 4 subsections)

For every figure/table:

```
In [Table/Fig X], [main observation with number].
[Expected or baseline comparison — e.g. vs random, vs thesis, vs other rung].
[Mechanistic reading — why this pattern is plausible given lab/montage/prior].
[Limitation or caveat in one clause if needed].
```

Subsections: **Cross-lab holdout performance** → **Laboratory heterogeneity** → **Substage structure and physiology** → **Methodological implications**.

### Conclusion (~120–180 words)

Three to five sentences; no new results. Methodological implications (vs thesis, QSLP-AE, limitations) belong in the last **Results and discussion** subsection, not here.

